From b0069fe3ab2d4974907be1da2b16281b749be9a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: darkmaniac7 <31073889+darkmaniac7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:08:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] firmware: release PEX_RST from a hardware alarm at
 exactly t = 0

Run on one card on 2026-11-20 as push1: releases landed 1 to 4 us
after t = 0 where the old step loop had slipped by up to +59 us,
except that the first release of every boot came 9 to 10 us late
(fixed in patch 0009).

The step loop blocks for every PMBus write (about 47 us measured), so a
write due at or just before t = 0 ran ahead of the release step and
pushed the release late by up to one write (pw 36, delay 117, td +81
released at about +59 us). The release is now a hardware alarm armed at
t0, at the highest IRQ priority on core 0; the release step is gone from
the timeline.

- The assert step stays where it was but is skipped if the release has
  already fired, so an overrunning step cannot leave the card in reset.
- After the timeline the firmware waits for the alarm (bounded), cancels
  it, releases the pin unconditionally and prints
  release_at=<us> scheduled=0 via=<alarm|fallback>.
- Before the shot, a "glitch WARN" line names every scheduled PMBus write
  whose [t, t + 47 us) window contains t = 0. The 36 us pw/gap floor is
  unchanged.
- Firmware marker fw=lab-psr1-push1 (fw=lab-psr1-push1-debug).

Builds for pico2_w (RP2350A and RP2350B) and pico2, normal and debug,
with no warnings.
